<title>SPAIN: CYCLING-RUTA DEL SOL SECOND STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-RUTA DEL SOL SECOND STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>PUENTE GENIL, Spain 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the second</p>
<p>stage of the Ruta del Sol between La Rinconada and Puente Genil</p>
<p>on Monday.</p>
<p>1. Johan Museeuw (Belgium) Mapei 4 hours 22 minutes 56 seconds</p>
<p>2. Erik Zabel (Germany) Germany</p>
<p>3. Viatcheslav Ekimov (Russia) U.S. Postal</p>
<p>4. Serguei Smetanine (Russia) Toscaf</p>
<p>5. Angelo Canzonieri (Italy) Saeco</p>
<p>6. Erik Dekker (Netherlands) Rabobank</p>
<p>7. Jo Planckaert (Belgium) Lotto</p>
<p>8. Marty Jemison (U.S.) U.S. Postal</p>
<p>9. Frankie Andreu (U.S.) Cofidis</p>
<p>10. Robbie McEwen (Australia) Rabobank  all same time</p>
<p>Overall standings:</p>
<p>1. Zabel		7 hours 8 minutes 7 seconds</p>
<p>2. Plankaert</p>
<p>3. Smetanine</p>
<p>4. Museeuw</p>
<p>5. McEwen</p>
<p>6. Angelo Canzonieri (Italy) Saeco</p>
<p>7. George Hincapie (U.S.) U.S. Postal</p>
<p>8. Biingen Fernandez (Spain) Euskadi</p>
<p>9. Andreu</p>
<p>10. Wilfrid Peeters (Belgium) Mapei     all same time</p>
